WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.378
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.648 --> 00:03.608
‎[theme music playing]

3
00:39.352 --> 00:43.064
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

4
00:43.147 --> 00:45.775
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTITIOUS AND DIFFERS FROM ‎ACTUAL MEDICAL PRACTICES AND REGULATIONS.

5
00:45.859 --> 00:48.069
‎CHARACTERS AND SETTINGS ARE FICTIONAL. ‎CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY.

6
00:48.736 --> 00:50.738
‎[fire crackling]

7
00:50.822 --> 00:52.824
‎[somber music playing]

8
01:16.848 --> 01:19.517
‎[gasping] No. No.

9
01:34.949 --> 01:35.783
‎Baraka.

10
01:42.415 --> 01:43.458
‎Baraka.

11
01:47.003 --> 01:48.421
‎One, two, three, four…

12
02:00.516 --> 02:01.517
‎Baraka.

13
02:02.352 --> 02:03.394
‎Baraka?

14
02:03.478 --> 02:04.979
‎[sniffles] Wake up.

15
02:06.481 --> 02:07.398
‎Baraka…

16
02:26.042 --> 02:28.002
‎[all crying]

17
02:52.026 --> 02:53.945
‎No!

18
02:54.028 --> 02:57.532
‎[sobbing]

19
02:59.075 --> 03:01.119
‎-[stew boiling] ‎-[Dr. Gye] Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

20
03:02.286 --> 03:03.538
‎Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

21
03:10.837 --> 03:11.963
‎The meat's going to burn.

22
03:12.046 --> 03:13.381
‎EPISODE 4

23
03:20.805 --> 03:22.682
‎Have I done something wrong?

24
03:23.891 --> 03:25.935
‎I don't know. You tell me. Have you?

25
03:26.019 --> 03:28.646
‎-No. ‎-You're acting like you have.

26
03:28.730 --> 03:29.897
‎No, I haven't.

27
03:29.981 --> 03:31.232
‎Come on. Dig in.

28
03:31.858 --> 03:32.734
‎[scoffs]

29
03:36.446 --> 03:37.280
‎Here.

30
03:38.489 --> 03:40.283
‎He can barely do an appendectomy, right?

31
03:40.950 --> 03:42.618
‎-Who? ‎-Well, who do you think?

32
03:43.202 --> 03:44.245
‎My name's Na Dae-il.

33
03:44.329 --> 03:46.414
‎I'll be joining the hospital ‎as a general surgeon as of today.

34
03:47.290 --> 03:48.166
‎Pleasure to meet you.

35
03:54.213 --> 03:56.507
‎The contract is on hold for now.

36
04:01.262 --> 04:04.223
‎[Dr. Do] Dr. Na has served his country ‎for a long time

37
04:04.307 --> 04:08.186
‎as a career military doctor, ‎after which he worked in the States,

38
04:08.269 --> 04:11.689
‎and has now come running ‎to answer his alma mater's call.

39
04:11.773 --> 04:14.150
‎[chuckles] He's such a fantastic surgeon.

40
04:14.692 --> 04:19.405
‎Dr. Gye I'd like you to remain in the ER ‎to help out. We're always short-staffed.

41
04:19.489 --> 04:21.282
‎MEDICAL SERVICE RATE SHEET

42
04:24.535 --> 04:28.748
‎Plenty of trauma cases in the military, ‎so at least he'll be decent at stitching.

43
04:28.831 --> 04:29.874
‎He's pretty good, actually.

44
04:30.458 --> 04:31.667
‎-You've seen his work? ‎-Mm-hmm.

45
04:32.293 --> 04:33.920
‎-A liver transplant. ‎-A liver?

46
04:35.088 --> 04:37.799
‎[sighs] I still can't believe ‎they stuck you in the ER

47
04:37.882 --> 04:39.384
‎after saving someone's life

48
04:39.467 --> 04:41.928
‎and rescuing them from a PR nightmare.

49
04:42.595 --> 04:44.389
‎After which, they held a press conference

50
04:44.472 --> 04:47.558
‎and put out a statement ‎taking credit for the whole thing.

51
04:47.642 --> 04:50.228
‎Auntie! Can I get ‎some more ‎ramyeon‎ noodles, please?

52
04:50.311 --> 04:53.022
‎-Auntie. ‎-‎Ramyeon‎ noodles? Go ahead, order some.

53
04:53.106 --> 04:54.857
‎Hurry up and eat. ‎They could page you any second.

54
04:55.525 --> 04:57.485
‎-Um, excuse me! ‎-No drinking.

55
04:57.985 --> 05:00.238
‎None at all, even if you can't sleep.

56
05:00.321 --> 05:01.364
‎[scoffs]

57
05:02.115 --> 05:03.157
‎I want you to know…

58
05:04.242 --> 05:05.410
‎this is ‎omija‎.

59
05:06.369 --> 05:08.538
‎It's from Eung-gu. It's my pacifier.

60
05:09.705 --> 05:10.748
‎Go ahead, smell it. Come on.

61
05:11.374 --> 05:12.750
‎We can't go back to that way of life.

62
05:13.960 --> 05:14.836
‎It's not right.

63
05:21.509 --> 05:23.177
‎Give me your coat. You're dripping on it.

64
05:29.016 --> 05:30.685
‎Don't get into trouble, okay?

65
05:30.768 --> 05:32.270
‎You're such a nag.

66
05:33.729 --> 05:35.022
‎Just lay low for now.

67
05:35.773 --> 05:36.941
‎They'll let you do surgeries again.

68
05:46.659 --> 05:47.493
‎Su-jeong!

69
05:54.458 --> 05:55.293
‎Stand up tall.

70
05:55.918 --> 05:57.211
‎Remember, you're Gye Su-jeong.

71
05:57.295 --> 05:59.505
‎Raised by me, Jang Hui-suk.

72
06:07.597 --> 06:10.183
‎[upbeat music playing]

73
06:14.937 --> 06:17.398
‎Pay us what you owe, ‎or I'll sue your pants off.

74
06:20.401 --> 06:21.611
‎I'll leave the melon for you.

75
06:21.694 --> 06:23.529
‎I'm sure you'll be calling me soon.

76
06:25.031 --> 06:25.990
‎It was nice meeting you.

77
06:30.703 --> 06:32.997
‎[chuckles] Such a good-looking guy.

78
06:36.959 --> 06:40.922
‎Yeesh. I wonder where they found ‎that shady bastard?

79
06:43.132 --> 06:46.302
‎Oh, that's the doctor ‎with the odd nickname.

80
06:46.385 --> 06:49.555
‎Oh, we were pretending not to see her, ‎but you must not have picked up on it.

81
06:49.639 --> 06:50.932
‎[chuckles]

82
06:51.015 --> 06:53.809
‎I never got to properly introduce myself ‎in the director's office.

83
06:54.310 --> 06:55.561
‎I've heard a lot about her, though.

84
06:56.520 --> 06:57.396
‎I think I'll say hello.

85
06:57.480 --> 06:59.565
‎No, no, she's not in our department.

86
06:59.649 --> 07:00.775
‎She won't return your greeting.

87
07:01.734 --> 07:03.986
‎There are a lot of things she won't do.

88
07:16.874 --> 07:17.959
‎Gye Su-jeong…

89
07:25.258 --> 07:26.634
‎-Put it down, put it down. ‎-Calm down.

90
07:26.717 --> 07:28.886
‎-No, just relax! Put the knife down! ‎-Put the knife down. Now!

91
07:28.970 --> 07:30.179
‎Put it down! Put it down!

92
07:30.263 --> 07:31.597
‎[assailant grunts]

93
07:32.515 --> 07:34.141
‎[whimpering]

94
07:35.101 --> 07:38.020
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

95
07:39.647 --> 07:42.858
‎[Dr. Mun] Unbelievable! ‎You had me talk to a patient

96
07:42.942 --> 07:46.529
‎so he could ask me a question ‎about something he read on the internet?

97
07:46.612 --> 07:47.780
‎You playing games?

98
07:47.863 --> 07:51.117
‎How dare you waste my valuable time ‎by having me talk to a patient!

99
07:52.159 --> 07:55.413
‎-Get out. Get out of here, you idiot. ‎-I'm so sorry. [grunts]

100
07:55.496 --> 07:57.582
‎Uh… I apologize.

101
08:10.845 --> 08:12.722
‎You sure are full of energy ‎so early in the morning,

102
08:12.805 --> 08:14.515
‎Dr. Mun Yeong-jong.

103
08:16.892 --> 08:18.978
‎Gotten pretty full of yourself, ‎huh, Na Dae-il?

104
08:19.061 --> 08:21.230
‎-Hmm. ‎-Took you long enough to come see me.

105
08:21.314 --> 08:22.356
‎Why is that?

106
08:22.440 --> 08:25.234
‎Oh, things have been so hectic. ‎Sorry about that.

107
08:26.402 --> 08:29.071
‎From being your student, I know how much ‎talking to patients annoys you.

108
08:29.155 --> 08:30.906
‎I guess that kid just didn't get the memo.

109
08:30.990 --> 08:33.242
‎I was already pissed off ‎because I had to work the night shift.

110
08:34.368 --> 08:36.495
‎If they just shut up ‎and let me get on with it,

111
08:36.579 --> 08:38.831
‎I'll do the surgery and save their lives.

112
08:38.914 --> 08:42.209
‎They don't know crap, but they ‎sure are happy to talk my ear off.

113
08:42.293 --> 08:43.586
‎Why do they do that? Geez.

114
08:45.463 --> 08:46.505
‎Why are you here?

115
08:47.590 --> 08:49.592
‎Oh, right. [clears throat]

116
09:01.228 --> 09:03.981
‎So, have you had breakfast?

117
09:07.902 --> 09:10.363
‎-[door opens] ‎-[sighs]

118
09:10.446 --> 09:11.530
‎Oh.

119
09:14.408 --> 09:18.245
‎Looks like he's been out for a while. ‎Yep, it's ice cold.

120
09:18.913 --> 09:21.540
‎Park Tae-gyeong. Hey, Park Tae-gyeong.

121
09:22.041 --> 09:23.751
‎Why is he sweating so much in his sleep?

122
09:24.794 --> 09:25.628
‎Dr. Park Tae-gyeong?

123
09:27.880 --> 09:29.298
‎Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

124
09:35.471 --> 09:36.764
‎Don't worry. I'm okay.

125
09:36.847 --> 09:39.850
‎[exhales] Were you actually sleeping ‎or just resting your eyes? Dude.

126
09:39.934 --> 09:41.352
‎Both at the same time.

127
09:42.061 --> 09:44.605
‎First thing I heard was, ‎"Yup, it's ice cold,"

128
09:44.689 --> 09:46.607
‎but I missed the right moment to get up.

129
09:47.191 --> 09:49.819
‎I never thought you would check my pupils.

130
09:49.902 --> 09:52.279
‎Oh, you were unresponsive ‎with a slight fever.

131
09:52.988 --> 09:55.241
‎-Sorry, buddy. ‎-[sighs] No worries.

132
09:55.324 --> 09:58.077
‎I dreamed I was doing an ABGA ‎and the artery ruptured.

133
09:58.160 --> 09:59.704
‎There was blood everywhere.

134
09:59.787 --> 10:03.290
‎Oh, well, ‎no wonder you broke out in cold sweat.

135
10:03.374 --> 10:04.959
‎I've had the same dream you had.

136
10:05.042 --> 10:07.545
‎Only it wasn't a dream.

137
10:07.628 --> 10:10.506
‎[Dr. Bae] What? Then you were the patient?

138
10:11.382 --> 10:14.343
‎Damn. I swear, this batch of interns ‎are all thumbs.

139
10:14.427 --> 10:16.387
‎[laughs] Just like the good old days.

140
10:17.680 --> 10:20.099
‎Actually, my arm wasn't ‎the worst casualty.

141
10:20.599 --> 10:23.436
‎My partner looked like ‎he might need a blood transfusion.

142
10:24.311 --> 10:26.605
‎The human body has so much blood in it…

143
10:27.440 --> 10:30.317
‎[Dr. Bae] On days like today, you need ‎something like ‎seonji‎ hangover soup.

144
10:30.401 --> 10:32.653
‎But first, throw that cold ‎ramyeon‎ away.

145
10:33.446 --> 10:34.447
‎Huh?

146
10:34.989 --> 10:37.324
‎[sighs] This was the last bowl of ‎ramyeon.

147
10:37.408 --> 10:40.202
‎We spend a third of our budget ‎just on wasted ‎ramyeon.

148
10:40.828 --> 10:43.998
‎Then I'll make a donation ‎to the budget for you, Tae-gyeong.

149
10:45.166 --> 10:48.919
‎-[Dr. Bae] Oh, no surprise there. Nice. ‎-[Dr. Na chuckles]

150
10:59.638 --> 11:01.766
‎Mmm! I'm starting to wake up now.

151
11:02.683 --> 11:04.185
‎[sighs]

152
11:05.102 --> 11:06.729
‎I bet Dr. Gye's okay, though.

153
11:06.812 --> 11:08.731
‎She's not an idiot like me. ‎That's for sure.

154
11:10.107 --> 11:11.108
‎[grunts]

155
11:11.192 --> 11:12.401
‎PATIENT (X) ‎DUMMY

156
11:12.485 --> 11:14.028
‎[Dr. Kim grunting] Oh, wow. Ow!

157
11:14.111 --> 11:15.362
‎ASSAILANT

158
11:15.446 --> 11:16.572
‎Wow, it really hurts.

159
11:17.072 --> 11:18.115
‎I think it's broken.

160
11:22.453 --> 11:23.370
‎Didn't you see the notice?

161
11:23.454 --> 11:25.039
‎It was in the group chat too.

162
11:25.122 --> 11:27.833
‎I even posted the training script ‎outlining the protocol to follow

163
11:27.917 --> 11:29.335
‎in case of violence in the ER.

164
11:30.294 --> 11:31.128
‎I get it.

165
11:31.795 --> 11:33.631
‎You missed it, ‎which is why you reacted that way.

166
11:33.714 --> 11:36.217
‎-You're a real troublemaker. ‎-Whoa.

167
11:36.800 --> 11:39.178
‎How can someone so violent ‎come into the emergency room…

168
11:40.846 --> 11:42.264
‎and save lives the way you do?

169
11:42.848 --> 11:44.808
‎They're gonna keep you here, aren't they?

170
11:44.892 --> 11:46.519
‎Thank goodness for that.

171
11:46.602 --> 11:50.314
‎It's just that we shouldn't be ‎where they send doctors for punishment.

172
11:50.397 --> 11:53.150
‎Why would they do that? ‎Do they look down on us or what?

173
11:54.818 --> 11:57.613
‎[clears throat] ‎Still, it's not so bad down here, huh?

174
11:58.447 --> 11:59.448
‎Wow.

175
11:59.949 --> 12:00.866
‎Wow! Wow!

176
12:00.950 --> 12:03.827
‎Dr. Gye, your hands are so fast! Amazing!

177
12:03.911 --> 12:05.496
‎[laughs]

178
12:05.579 --> 12:07.831
‎Actually, we haven't cast ‎the assailant yet,

179
12:07.915 --> 12:08.958
‎which is why I was doing it.

180
12:09.625 --> 12:11.585
‎They're going to shoot ‎a promo for the hospital.

181
12:11.669 --> 12:13.796
‎And the press will be there as well, ‎and I thought that you might--

182
12:13.879 --> 12:14.880
‎That's not something I do.

183
12:15.381 --> 12:17.925
‎Your part would be ‎to just lie quietly in Bed 7

184
12:18.008 --> 12:19.385
‎to avoid any trouble.

185
12:19.468 --> 12:22.263
‎Well, okay. ‎You need to rehearse beforehand.

186
12:22.346 --> 12:24.640
‎So if there's an incident, ‎you can respond quickly.

187
12:24.723 --> 12:27.101
‎And you haven't even heard the best yet. ‎Want me to tell you?

188
12:27.184 --> 12:28.310
‎Not really. Why would I?

189
12:29.603 --> 12:31.438
‎The best part is that I am the director.

190
12:32.022 --> 12:34.608
‎I played Macduff ‎in the 95th production of ‎Macbeth

191
12:34.692 --> 12:37.444
‎as a member of Guseo University's ‎Dramatic Art Society!

192
12:37.528 --> 12:40.364
‎-The dramatic what? ‎-It's a theater club.

193
12:40.447 --> 12:42.908
‎-What'd you call me for? ‎-Bravo!

194
12:44.451 --> 12:47.037
‎You've just been cast ‎as the hostage. Congratulations. Bravo!

195
12:47.121 --> 12:47.955
‎What?

196
12:48.038 --> 12:51.125
‎Dr. Jo, only you can convey the delicate, ‎fragile quality of the hostage

197
12:51.208 --> 12:52.835
‎along with the tragedy of the moment,

198
12:52.918 --> 12:54.420
‎and still truly express--

199
12:54.503 --> 12:56.755
‎She's not the type ‎that would be taken hostage.

200
12:56.839 --> 12:57.923
‎Shh.

201
12:58.882 --> 13:00.676
‎-I'm leaving. I need to go. ‎-No, don't. Please.

202
13:00.759 --> 13:02.928
‎You're the only one in the hospital ‎who's got that vibe.

203
13:03.012 --> 13:04.555
‎Dr. Kim Seong-jin?

204
13:04.638 --> 13:07.224
‎Dr. Cha wants you to check your email.

205
13:07.308 --> 13:08.767
‎-Oh! ‎-[grunts]

206
13:09.518 --> 13:10.561
‎Check your email.

207
13:11.812 --> 13:14.189
‎What's wrong with you? ‎How many days have you gone without sleep?

208
13:14.273 --> 13:16.900
‎Is this what they call street casting?

209
13:16.984 --> 13:21.071
‎Uh, it's been three or four days? ‎Although, earlier I slept a little bit.

210
13:21.155 --> 13:22.239
‎No, don't sleep at all!

211
13:22.323 --> 13:24.658
‎You're young. Half a day of sleep ‎and you'll be as good as new,

212
13:24.742 --> 13:25.826
‎then you'll lose the look.

213
13:25.909 --> 13:27.536
‎I have no idea what you're talking about.

214
13:27.620 --> 13:28.454
‎Okay, okay, okay.

215
13:28.537 --> 13:30.914
‎Why don't we go over there ‎and practice a few lines?

216
13:30.998 --> 13:32.333
‎Hi there, Dr. Jo.

217
13:32.416 --> 13:34.168
‎Dr. Gye, I have a lot to tell you.

218
13:35.127 --> 13:37.212
‎Dr. Kim seems much better than usual.

219
13:37.296 --> 13:39.173
‎[Dr. Gye] That's him doing better?

220
13:39.256 --> 13:40.674
‎He probably needs a brain scan.

221
13:41.258 --> 13:44.803
‎We usually refer ‎to that type of behavior as "excitement."

222
13:45.888 --> 13:50.017
‎If it's called ‎Macbeth‎, that means ‎the main character must be Macbeth.

223
13:50.893 --> 13:52.061
‎Macduff…

224
13:53.520 --> 13:54.813
‎I wonder if they're related.

225
13:54.897 --> 13:55.898
‎Are you…

226
13:56.982 --> 13:58.901
‎serious right now?

227
13:58.984 --> 14:01.945
‎Oh, so you think all Macs ‎are related, huh?

228
14:02.821 --> 14:05.616
‎Then you must think the hamburger place ‎was founded by their--

229
14:05.699 --> 14:07.826
‎What? I never thought about that.

230
14:10.704 --> 14:11.830
‎You're a genius.

231
14:11.914 --> 14:15.042
‎You sure can drag me down ‎to your level quickly. It's annoying.

232
14:16.168 --> 14:19.505
‎It has been so quiet in the ER. ‎Why don't you go home early today--

233
14:19.588 --> 14:21.674
‎-[siren wailing] ‎-[Dr. Kim] I wish you hadn't said that.

234
14:24.718 --> 14:26.637
‎-Trauma patient. ‎-What happened?

235
14:26.720 --> 14:28.138
‎Five workers fell from the third floor

236
14:28.222 --> 14:30.224
‎after a construction site ‎retaining wall collapsed.

237
14:30.307 --> 14:31.433
‎They all fell onto a tree.

238
14:31.517 --> 14:33.978
‎Four of them are conscious. ‎This guy's the only one who isn't.

239
14:34.687 --> 14:36.605
‎And his blood pressure keeps dropping.

240
14:36.689 --> 14:38.148
‎Get a CT first. Notify the OR.

241
14:38.232 --> 14:39.316
‎[Dr. Park] Okay, will do.

242
14:39.400 --> 14:42.319
‎[dramatic music playing]

243
14:42.403 --> 14:44.738
‎-Is he from the construction site? ‎-Yeah, he is.

244
14:44.822 --> 14:45.656
‎Hang in there.

245
14:54.581 --> 14:56.542
‎The ground beneath me just crumbled away.

246
14:56.625 --> 14:58.252
‎I was a Marine, so I'm quick.

247
14:58.335 --> 15:00.921
‎I grabbed onto whatever ‎I could see and just--

248
15:01.005 --> 15:02.047
‎[shouts]

249
15:10.806 --> 15:13.100
‎[stapler clicking]

250
15:19.064 --> 15:20.899
‎Whoa!

251
15:21.608 --> 15:24.403
‎Well, you did it again, huh?

252
15:24.486 --> 15:27.281
‎[laughs] That was quick. Wasn't it? Right?

253
15:28.073 --> 15:30.159
‎You've really got a knack for the ER, huh?

254
15:30.242 --> 15:33.328
‎A knack for the ER. You're a game-changer. ‎That's what you are.

255
15:33.412 --> 15:34.496
‎[laughs]

256
15:35.330 --> 15:37.249
‎Now, let me just relax ‎for a minute then--

257
15:37.875 --> 15:38.709
‎Huh?

258
15:39.168 --> 15:40.669
‎What's wrong? Where are you going?

259
15:40.753 --> 15:42.713
‎Dr. Gye? Dr. Gye?

260
15:43.338 --> 15:44.548
‎A real game-changer!

261
15:44.631 --> 15:45.507
‎HAN JI-HUN, 42 Y/O, M

262
15:45.591 --> 15:47.760
‎[monitors beeping]

263
15:47.843 --> 15:49.720
‎[Dr. Do] ‎The CT shows that the liver's bleeding.

264
15:49.803 --> 15:52.181
‎Looks like we'll have to scoop it out.

265
15:53.724 --> 15:55.100
‎-[Dr. Park] The blood… ‎-[Dr. Do] Hey! Let's go!

266
15:56.101 --> 15:57.978
‎[Dr. Park] Uh, right. [clears throat]

267
15:58.062 --> 16:00.731
‎There's so much blood. It's…

268
16:01.899 --> 16:05.319
‎-Oh, Dr. Gye Su-jeong. ‎-[Dr. Do] What? What's she doing here?

269
16:07.321 --> 16:08.781
‎[Dr. Jo] ‎How many units of RBCs do we have?

270
16:08.864 --> 16:10.449
‎-[Dr. Do] Come on. Hurry up. ‎-[Dr. Park] Oh, okay.

271
16:11.617 --> 16:12.701
‎I mean, this…

272
16:13.368 --> 16:15.079
‎Uh, this…

273
16:15.162 --> 16:17.790
‎-Hey! What's the problem? Get it together. ‎-[Dr. Park] Uh, I'm sorry.

274
16:20.959 --> 16:22.586
‎Uh, oh, Dr. Gye.

275
16:22.669 --> 16:24.671
‎[Dr. Do] What are you doing? ‎This isn't your patient.

276
16:24.755 --> 16:25.881
‎Go back to the ER.

277
16:28.801 --> 16:30.719
‎What the hell's going on? Seriously!

278
16:42.439 --> 16:45.025
‎-[Dr. Park] Whoa, whoa, whoa, Dr. Gye. ‎-[Dr. Do] What? Hey.

279
16:49.822 --> 16:52.699
‎[monitor beeping]

280
16:54.409 --> 16:55.661
‎BP is stabilizing.

281
16:55.744 --> 16:58.372
‎[Dr. Do] The bleeding is under control.

282
17:02.126 --> 17:03.502
‎[Dr. Na] So now…

283
17:06.421 --> 17:07.631
‎Hmm.

284
17:09.550 --> 17:11.301
‎Mm-hmm. [chuckles]

285
17:17.432 --> 17:18.892
‎Just like I thought.

286
17:21.228 --> 17:22.146
‎I found it.

287
17:34.116 --> 17:35.492
‎[Dr. Gye] If you found it, suture it.

288
17:42.416 --> 17:43.709
‎[Dr. Na chuckles]

289
17:44.877 --> 17:45.919
‎Suturing.

290
17:46.003 --> 17:48.046
‎-Suction. ‎-[Dr. Park] Oh, uh…

291
17:50.048 --> 17:51.758
‎Prepare 5-0 Prolene.

292
17:54.428 --> 17:56.346
‎[Chairman Kim] ‎Director Bu, you never struck me as…

293
17:57.014 --> 17:58.432
‎such an impetuous person.

294
17:59.391 --> 18:01.226
‎[Director Bu] ‎We were just trying to save the hospital.

295
18:01.310 --> 18:02.728
‎We didn't mean anything by it.

296
18:03.395 --> 18:05.981
‎If our hospital gets on ‎the public's bad side again…

297
18:06.523 --> 18:08.734
‎And what about our bad side? ‎Doesn't that concern you?

298
18:08.817 --> 18:11.778
‎Oh, we wouldn't dare do that. ‎Not that we're not concerned.

299
18:11.862 --> 18:13.488
‎We'd just never even consider it.

300
18:13.572 --> 18:16.783
‎If we'd known, we'd never have done it. ‎We were just impulsive.

301
18:16.867 --> 18:17.993
‎It was the former director's blunder?

302
18:18.952 --> 18:20.454
‎Cooperate with the appeal? ‎What the hell is that?

303
18:21.830 --> 18:24.833
‎How could you set such a precedent? ‎This affects every hospital out there.

304
18:25.459 --> 18:26.585
‎[stammers] You're right.

305
18:27.794 --> 18:28.879
‎Yes, you're right.

306
18:28.962 --> 18:32.299
‎Those hospitals can do ‎the same thing we did then.

307
18:34.676 --> 18:35.719
‎What?

308
18:35.802 --> 18:39.431
‎If we had heard them out from the start ‎and welcomed their investigators

309
18:39.514 --> 18:41.308
‎and cooperated with them,

310
18:41.391 --> 18:45.229
‎or even simply offered our condolences ‎to the family of the victim,

311
18:46.605 --> 18:48.315
‎do you think it would have come to this?

312
18:48.398 --> 18:51.109
‎Apologies, Chairman. ‎We didn't mean to offend.

313
18:51.193 --> 18:53.862
‎And I assure you, we will go apologize ‎to the members of Magnolia.

314
18:59.826 --> 19:00.661
‎Now is the time

315
19:01.995 --> 19:05.374
‎for all of us doctors to come together ‎and unite, and you people

316
19:05.457 --> 19:07.000
‎go out there and pull that stunt?

317
19:07.084 --> 19:09.461
‎I'm cutting off all support ‎to this hospital as of now!

318
19:09.544 --> 19:12.631
‎[stammering] You know the hospital ‎is struggling just to make ends meet.

319
19:12.714 --> 19:14.341
‎We had to do it to survive.

320
19:14.424 --> 19:16.635
‎We're barely managing to keep ‎our doors open,

321
19:16.718 --> 19:19.054
‎thanks to your support ‎and coordination, Chairman.

322
19:23.141 --> 19:24.559
‎Won't you please reconsider?

323
19:26.478 --> 19:29.648
‎Well, you made such a stink ‎about being short-staffed and all,

324
19:29.731 --> 19:32.526
‎so I sent you a carefully selected ‎and very talented doctor.

325
19:33.110 --> 19:34.903
‎And you didn't even thank me.

326
19:36.029 --> 19:38.031
‎So, how do you like Dr. Na? ‎He's good, isn't he?

327
19:38.115 --> 19:40.742
‎Oh! He's truly amazing.

328
19:41.243 --> 19:44.913
‎So skilled as a doctor, ‎and also a really good guy.

329
19:44.997 --> 19:48.625
‎He seems all right so far, ‎but it's a little early to tell for sure.

330
19:51.211 --> 19:52.629
‎I'm very grateful, though.

331
19:55.465 --> 19:58.427
‎The mayor and I will be dropping by ‎here soon, so get ready for that.

332
19:58.510 --> 20:00.012
‎And the purpose of your visit?

333
20:00.095 --> 20:01.763
‎[Director Bu] ‎Oh, of course, he should come.

334
20:01.847 --> 20:04.391
‎After all, we're the region's ‎most important hospital.

335
20:04.474 --> 20:06.351
‎What should we do to prepare for you?

336
20:06.977 --> 20:09.354
‎[Chairman Kim] ‎You should know the drill by now. [scoffs]

337
20:09.438 --> 20:12.441
‎[Director Bu] Oh, there was no children's ‎hospital back when the mayor worked here.

338
20:12.524 --> 20:15.193
‎-So it might be a good idea to do a tour? ‎-[Chairman Kim] That sounds good.

339
20:15.277 --> 20:16.111
‎[Director Bu] Great.

340
20:17.362 --> 20:19.031
‎[Chairman Kim] ‎Everyone is struggling these days.

341
20:19.614 --> 20:22.451
‎You think we're giving you money ‎because we've got too much lying around?

342
20:22.534 --> 20:23.994
‎-[phone buzzes] ‎-[Director Bu] We'll do our best.

343
20:24.077 --> 20:26.455
‎-[Chairman Kim] Do our best, my ass. ‎-[Director Bu chuckles weakly]

344
20:26.538 --> 20:27.873
‎TIME TO ADMINISTER EYE DROPS

345
20:30.667 --> 20:32.544
‎Oh. Thank you for your hard work.

346
20:32.627 --> 20:34.713
‎No worries. ‎It was pretty routine. [chuckles]

347
20:34.796 --> 20:38.216
‎And that doctor, Snake Su-jeong, ‎did the important part.

348
20:38.300 --> 20:39.551
‎Oh…

349
20:40.427 --> 20:42.346
‎Just kidding. [chuckles]

350
20:42.429 --> 20:43.263
‎Everyone calls her that,

351
20:43.347 --> 20:47.517
‎-so I thought I'd give it a whirl. ‎-Oh. Oh, you must have been offended.

352
20:47.601 --> 20:49.770
‎She didn't mean to intrude ‎during your surgery.

353
20:49.853 --> 20:51.980
‎Sometimes she just leaps before she looks.

354
20:52.064 --> 20:55.901
‎Hmm, you're the only one who talks about ‎Dr. Gye with any real decency.

355
20:56.485 --> 20:57.986
‎Oh, is that so?

356
20:59.363 --> 21:02.157
‎-I guess they are pretty disrespectful. ‎-Oh?

357
21:03.492 --> 21:04.576
‎Your face just dropped.

358
21:05.410 --> 21:06.244
‎Are you guys close?

359
21:06.328 --> 21:07.954
‎Huh? Oh, no.

360
21:08.914 --> 21:13.251
‎Uh, it wouldn't be accurate ‎to describe us as close.

361
21:13.835 --> 21:14.795
‎I better get going.

362
21:16.671 --> 21:18.090
‎I'd like to use that word.

363
21:19.508 --> 21:20.884
‎"Close," I mean.

364
21:22.135 --> 21:23.220
‎In regard to…

365
21:24.805 --> 21:26.014
‎Dr. Gye and me.

366
21:27.766 --> 21:29.142
‎I hope you could ‎help me out with that.

367
21:31.311 --> 21:33.188
‎[typing]

368
21:44.324 --> 21:46.868
‎Why would you march ‎into someone else's OR like that, huh?

369
21:50.163 --> 21:53.208
‎Do you think Ms. Jang Hui-suk from ‎the temp agency has heard about it yet?

370
21:54.167 --> 21:55.001
‎Oh, shit.

371
21:56.628 --> 21:59.256
‎People are talking about it ‎differently this time.

372
21:59.339 --> 22:00.382
‎It was no big deal.

373
22:00.465 --> 22:02.843
‎The surgery was successful ‎and the patient is okay.

374
22:04.094 --> 22:06.221
‎Anything interesting ‎concerning Dr. Na Dae-il?

375
22:06.304 --> 22:07.514
‎We didn't get into a fight.

376
22:07.597 --> 22:10.559
‎Bingo! There you go. ‎That's not logical, is it?

377
22:10.642 --> 22:12.102
‎You barge into his OR,

378
22:12.185 --> 22:14.729
‎he's supposed to throw scissors ‎at the wall or swear up and down at you,

379
22:14.813 --> 22:16.398
‎make a scene and kick you out.

380
22:16.481 --> 22:19.693
‎It's that he smiled. Who does that? ‎Crazy, isn't it?

381
22:19.776 --> 22:21.278
‎[Dr. Na] Is it that crazy?

382
22:21.361 --> 22:23.405
‎[chuckles weakly] Uh…

383
22:23.488 --> 22:26.199
‎There's gotta be soundproof carpet ‎in front of the ER desk.

384
22:26.283 --> 22:28.368
‎Everyone keeps sneaking up on me.

385
22:28.451 --> 22:31.454
‎Oh, um, nice to meet you. ‎You're Dr. Na Dae-il, aren't you?

386
22:32.080 --> 22:33.206
‎Pleasure meeting you.

387
22:33.290 --> 22:34.583
‎You must be Dr. Kim Seong-jin.

388
22:34.666 --> 22:35.959
‎I think so, yeah.

389
22:36.751 --> 22:39.838
‎Oh, as the head of the ER, ‎it's my fault that Dr. Gye here

390
22:39.921 --> 22:42.632
‎caused a scene in your OR. ‎I'm deeply apologetic.

391
22:42.716 --> 22:45.260
‎-Please go easy on her. ‎-[chuckles]

392
22:45.343 --> 22:47.929
‎No, please, cause another scene.

393
22:48.013 --> 22:49.014
‎[Dr. Kim] Huh?

394
22:49.097 --> 22:51.975
‎After seeing the CT scan, ‎she knew what needed to be done.

395
22:52.058 --> 22:53.226
‎And she was right.

396
22:54.227 --> 22:55.395
‎Ah…

397
22:59.316 --> 23:01.193
‎Dr. Jo, emergency at the ER desk.

398
23:01.276 --> 23:02.527
‎Come diagnose the situation here.

399
23:03.987 --> 23:06.656
‎But I knew it too.

400
23:07.282 --> 23:11.286
‎I just missed my opportunity ‎due to your dynamic entrance. [laughs]

401
23:18.585 --> 23:20.879
‎Dr. Gye, I know you're busy working,

402
23:20.962 --> 23:24.299
‎but why don't you show some appreciation ‎for what Dr. Na brought?

403
23:24.382 --> 23:26.551
‎-There's bread too. Oh, wow. ‎-[siren ringer plays]

404
23:27.594 --> 23:29.846
‎[Dr. Jo] ‎I'm an anesthesiologist.

405
23:29.930 --> 23:31.640
‎You're no fun, Won-jin. No fun.

406
23:32.474 --> 23:36.144
‎I may not look it, ‎but my pride isn't easily injured.

407
23:37.646 --> 23:40.774
‎But still, it's impressive that you ‎figured it out as quickly as you did.

408
23:49.991 --> 23:52.410
‎Dr. Park Tae-gyeong told me ‎you liked this kind of stuff.

409
23:52.494 --> 23:54.246
‎Is that not true? ‎Did I buy the wrong thing?

410
23:54.329 --> 23:56.581
‎Mmm! No, it's delicious.

411
23:56.665 --> 23:57.707
‎Yeah.

412
23:58.833 --> 24:00.210
‎Why are you staring?

413
24:05.340 --> 24:06.299
‎What are you looking at?

414
24:06.383 --> 24:08.510
‎Oh, yeah, you're standing ‎where she always looks.

415
24:08.593 --> 24:09.594
‎Sorry?

416
24:10.262 --> 24:11.763
‎-I'll be going no. ‎-Yeah. See you.

417
24:13.223 --> 24:14.975
‎Where is Dr. Gye Su-jeong going?

418
24:15.475 --> 24:16.476
‎Oh, home. She's clocking out.

419
24:19.229 --> 24:20.105
‎Ah, right.

420
24:21.940 --> 24:23.400
‎That's right. Mm-hmm.

421
24:23.483 --> 24:24.693
‎Right on time.

422
24:28.321 --> 24:29.322
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

423
24:29.406 --> 24:32.993
‎RECOVERY ROOM

424
24:44.963 --> 24:46.715
‎Oh, Dr. Na, what brings you here?

425
24:50.093 --> 24:52.304
‎Oh, do you want me to call her over here?

426
24:52.387 --> 24:53.305
‎No, thank you.

427
24:54.639 --> 24:56.141
‎That's the first patient to be listed…

428
24:56.224 --> 24:57.058
‎YEO JEONG-SUN

429
24:57.142 --> 24:59.269
‎…under Dr. Gye Su-jeong's name.

430
24:59.352 --> 25:02.981
‎Oh! This is the craniotomy she did. ‎Is that true?

431
25:03.064 --> 25:04.190
‎Mm-hmm, yeah.

432
25:04.274 --> 25:07.444
‎It's not actually the first surgery ‎she did. It's just the first one--

433
25:07.527 --> 25:08.653
‎I heard she was fast.

434
25:09.779 --> 25:11.781
‎-Yeah. ‎-How fast?

435
25:11.865 --> 25:14.242
‎Fast enough that no one ‎really wants to talk about it much.

436
25:16.286 --> 25:17.120
‎Really?

437
25:17.746 --> 25:21.583
‎Last time, they switched surgeons ‎from Dr. Do to Dr. Gye,

438
25:21.666 --> 25:24.419
‎so this patient ‎isn't really her first, but still.

439
25:24.502 --> 25:26.296
‎From the start, she…

440
25:28.631 --> 25:29.466
‎What's his deal?

441
25:34.429 --> 25:36.139
‎YEO JEONG-SUN ‎PRIMARY: GYE SU-JEONG

442
26:03.333 --> 26:05.335
‎-[dings] ‎-[laughs]

443
26:05.418 --> 26:07.796
‎So, you got off work, then what?

444
26:07.879 --> 26:10.048
‎What could be more romantic ‎than two doctors

445
26:10.131 --> 26:12.384
‎dipping their hands ‎into a blood-filled abdomen?

446
26:12.467 --> 26:13.968
‎So sweet!

447
26:14.052 --> 26:16.012
‎And together, they staunched the bleeding.

448
26:16.096 --> 26:18.056
‎Oh, they should have done ‎the ligation together too.

449
26:18.139 --> 26:19.808
‎-Can we play? ‎-He didn't follow you?

450
26:19.891 --> 26:21.601
‎Yeah, did he chase after you?

451
26:23.186 --> 26:24.020
‎Who?

452
26:24.104 --> 26:25.855
‎-Come on, you know who. ‎-Are you serious?

453
26:25.939 --> 26:28.316
‎-Hey, you're a moron. You're such a moron. ‎-You really are a silly kid.

454
26:28.400 --> 26:30.402
‎-Completely silly. ‎-You know if this guy was in the military,

455
26:30.485 --> 26:33.446
‎then he's got to be ‎a pretty decent, upstanding person.

456
26:33.530 --> 26:34.823
‎You know, right?

457
26:34.906 --> 26:36.366
‎Oh!

458
26:36.449 --> 26:38.868
‎-He's stunning. Look at him. ‎-Whoa!

459
26:38.952 --> 26:40.203
‎-Whoa! ‎-[laughing]

460
26:40.286 --> 26:42.705
‎-Oh, be still my heart! ‎-He's a pretty boy, huh?

461
26:42.789 --> 26:44.999
‎-He got your number, right? ‎-What number?

462
26:45.083 --> 26:48.503
‎Man, you South Koreans need to step it up. ‎He get your digits, or what?

463
26:48.586 --> 26:51.506
‎Wow, so what makes you so cool?

464
26:52.215 --> 26:54.801
‎Hey, there's a lot more ‎where that came from.

465
26:55.427 --> 26:56.636
‎"I ate and left no crumbs."

466
26:57.595 --> 26:59.222
‎"Never mind. I can't even." [scoffs]

467
26:59.305 --> 27:00.140
‎What?

468
27:01.182 --> 27:02.892
‎That guy's hands smell fishy.

469
27:04.394 --> 27:05.895
‎The smell is way too familiar.

470
27:07.355 --> 27:09.732
‎"Let's shut our traps and give it a go."

471
27:09.816 --> 27:11.609
‎-What's that? ‎-I said, "Shut--"

472
27:13.111 --> 27:14.487
‎I heard the patient lived.

473
27:15.488 --> 27:17.365
‎You said the hospital didn't call you.

474
27:17.449 --> 27:19.659
‎Come on. Is there anything ‎she doesn't know?

475
27:19.784 --> 27:22.036
‎Inside the hospital, Ms. Jang knows all.

476
27:22.120 --> 27:23.163
‎Crap.

477
27:24.205 --> 27:26.458
‎He smells fishy? And not like money?

478
27:27.125 --> 27:28.626
‎Well, money smells fishy.

479
27:29.836 --> 27:32.088
‎-[laughs] ‎-[all] No! Ugh.

480
27:35.133 --> 27:36.134
‎[gasps]

481
27:40.346 --> 27:44.017
‎Oh, no. This is Dr. Ma's book. ‎He's gonna kill me.

482
27:58.656 --> 28:00.742
‎[Dr. Ma] ‎But as an intern, ‎just quietly finish your month with us

483
28:00.825 --> 28:01.659
‎and then go on your way.

484
28:01.743 --> 28:03.620
‎I really don't want to see ‎any more interns

485
28:03.703 --> 28:05.538
‎doing a rotation in surgery ‎pretending to be doctors

486
28:05.622 --> 28:07.248
‎with some great sense of duty only to…

487
28:08.249 --> 28:09.959
‎go to an easier department somewhere.

488
28:10.543 --> 28:12.128
‎You won't be a surgeon anyway.

489
28:16.257 --> 28:17.842
‎[Dr. Park] This damn blood…

490
28:17.926 --> 28:19.636
‎I'm sick of it already.

491
28:20.386 --> 28:22.430
‎And I want to be a doctor. How pathetic.

492
28:24.307 --> 28:25.767
‎[sighs] God.

493
28:29.229 --> 28:31.231
‎YEO JEONG-SUN

494
28:44.494 --> 28:45.745
‎She's using that already?

495
28:48.957 --> 28:49.874
‎She's amazing.

496
29:02.470 --> 29:05.807
‎[clears throat] It's time to go to school.

497
29:06.850 --> 29:07.851
‎[grunts]

498
29:09.435 --> 29:10.436
‎Oh.

499
29:11.354 --> 29:12.730
‎Hey, have a…

500
29:12.814 --> 29:14.566
‎Have a good day! See you--

501
29:19.612 --> 29:20.655
‎[groans]

502
29:22.824 --> 29:23.950
‎ANTACIDS

503
29:30.957 --> 29:32.834
‎DESTINATION: ‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

504
29:37.881 --> 29:39.132
‎Dr. Gye Su-Jeong!

505
29:42.176 --> 29:43.428
‎[sighs]

506
29:44.220 --> 29:46.806
‎I want to finish what I was saying ‎yesterday in the elevator.

507
29:49.392 --> 29:52.145
‎[chuckles] Okay.

508
30:02.322 --> 30:05.325
‎The operation was completed incorrectly. ‎When that rupture happens,

509
30:05.408 --> 30:06.826
‎it'll be on your watch.

510
30:06.910 --> 30:08.745
‎If not, then I'll hand ‎my white coat to you.

511
30:08.828 --> 30:10.204
‎Yeah, sure, I'll throw mine in too.

512
30:10.288 --> 30:12.582
‎Let's hope he's wrong, ‎and I know he's not. You better be sure.

513
30:12.665 --> 30:16.210
‎Min-gu, you threatening my career ‎doesn't scare me at all.

514
30:18.296 --> 30:19.505
‎Polish your resumes.

515
30:51.621 --> 30:52.538
‎[clears throat]

516
30:53.498 --> 30:55.917
‎They moved the patient ‎to the general ward,

517
30:56.000 --> 30:58.002
‎which means the aneurysm didn't rupture.

518
31:33.121 --> 31:34.080
‎[Dr. Park] ‎See you later.

519
31:35.540 --> 31:38.960
‎BUIL DINER

520
31:39.043 --> 31:40.712
‎Oh! We'll get the next open table.

521
31:40.795 --> 31:45.675
‎We've been waiting 20 minutes already. ‎I hate waiting in line to eat like this.

522
31:45.758 --> 31:47.385
‎Why'd you drag me out here anyway?

523
31:47.468 --> 31:49.804
‎Relax, enjoy the nice weather.

524
31:49.887 --> 31:53.516
‎This is my way of welcoming ‎Dr. Gye to the ER department.

525
31:53.599 --> 31:55.351
‎Then you should have eaten ‎with the ER team.

526
31:55.435 --> 31:56.561
‎Why'd you ask Dr. Park and me?

527
31:56.644 --> 31:59.439
‎Well, I mean, we're always so busy, ‎we have to take turns eating.

528
31:59.522 --> 32:03.026
‎And I thought that it would be nice ‎to eat together for a change.

529
32:03.109 --> 32:05.862
‎So I begged another doctor to cover us ‎so we could all go out.

530
32:06.529 --> 32:07.864
‎Ah! Ah!

531
32:07.947 --> 32:11.743
‎I-- I heard about that run-in you had, ‎you know, what happened in the elevator.

532
32:11.826 --> 32:13.995
‎You know? You know this? [laughs]

533
32:14.078 --> 32:15.288
‎I felt a little, you know.

534
32:15.371 --> 32:18.499
‎[laughs] And you two helped get ‎Dr. Gye into the ER,

535
32:18.583 --> 32:20.418
‎so I thought I might as well ‎invite you guys also.

536
32:21.335 --> 32:23.796
‎Well, I guess I can't argue with that.

537
32:24.922 --> 32:27.967
‎Whoa, whoa, whoa! ‎You're not backing out now, are you?

538
32:28.051 --> 32:29.302
‎Stick it out. Just wait a sec.

539
32:30.261 --> 32:32.972
‎[sighs] The only reason I came ‎is 'cause you're buying.

540
32:33.056 --> 32:35.141
‎-Wait, you're buying? ‎-[clears throat]

541
32:35.224 --> 32:38.561
‎Dr. Gye is my one-woman army. ‎It's the least I could do.

542
32:38.644 --> 32:41.314
‎Why don't you cut ties ‎with those damn surgeons

543
32:41.397 --> 32:42.857
‎and keep working in the ER with me?

544
32:42.940 --> 32:43.816
‎[chuckles]

545
32:44.776 --> 32:47.570
‎What's his deal? ‎He seems like a pretty hard worker, huh?

546
32:47.653 --> 32:50.948
‎But he always looks so weak and frail.

547
32:51.032 --> 32:52.158
‎He needs herbal medicine.

548
32:52.241 --> 32:54.410
‎Says a Western medicine practitioner.

549
32:54.494 --> 32:56.704
‎Come on, we all know that, as kids,

550
32:56.788 --> 32:58.956
‎our grandmothers' cures ‎were nothing short of miraculous.

551
32:59.040 --> 33:01.834
‎It's taking so long because ‎we're waiting for a table for four.

552
33:01.918 --> 33:03.127
‎We should sit two per table.

553
33:03.211 --> 33:04.879
‎What are you talking about?

554
33:04.962 --> 33:06.714
‎Look, the point was to eat together.

555
33:06.798 --> 33:08.716
‎It defeats the purpose ‎if we sit separately.

556
33:08.800 --> 33:10.760
‎[sighs] Yeah, ‎but if someone comes out alone,

557
33:10.843 --> 33:12.136
‎I'll take their table.

558
33:12.887 --> 33:15.139
‎It's actually nice ‎sitting outside like this.

559
33:15.223 --> 33:17.141
‎I'm always in the hospital at this hour.

560
33:19.185 --> 33:20.770
‎Oh! There's a table. Let's go!

561
33:20.853 --> 33:22.647
‎There's a table! Let's go! ‎There's a table now!

562
33:22.730 --> 33:23.898
‎[groaning]

563
33:26.317 --> 33:28.069
‎-Are you okay? ‎-[groaning]

564
33:28.152 --> 33:29.904
‎-What's the matter? ‎-Mr. Kwon?

565
33:31.948 --> 33:32.949
‎[Dr. Do] He's not picking up.

566
33:33.032 --> 33:34.492
‎KWON CHUNG-HYEON ‎UGANG PHARMACEUTICALS

567
33:34.575 --> 33:35.952
‎That's not like him at all.

568
33:36.035 --> 33:39.372
‎I know, right? He always calls ‎if he's late, even five minutes.

569
33:39.455 --> 33:40.915
‎Maybe he's passed out somewhere.

570
33:40.998 --> 33:43.251
‎Sometimes pharmaceutical reps ‎are so hungover

571
33:43.334 --> 33:44.961
‎from drinking with clients all night

572
33:45.044 --> 33:46.963
‎that they sleep it off in their cars.

573
33:47.046 --> 33:48.131
‎Uh, not Mr. Kwon.

574
33:48.798 --> 33:50.883
‎One time, there was a seminar ‎in the province.

575
33:50.967 --> 33:52.176
‎Mmm! Mm-hmm!

576
33:52.260 --> 33:56.055
‎Afterward, he treated us to a round of ‎golf, 18 holes, and an expensive dinner.

577
33:56.139 --> 33:58.266
‎And at the bar, we mixed liquor and beer.

578
33:58.349 --> 34:00.351
‎Oh, Mr. Kwon's liquor-and-beer mix ‎is so good!

579
34:00.434 --> 34:02.979
‎[all cheering, exclaiming]

580
34:03.062 --> 34:05.481
‎[all chanting] Do Yun-sik!

581
34:07.984 --> 34:09.652
‎-[pop music playing] ‎-I'm rooting for us!

582
34:09.735 --> 34:12.572
‎[all cheering]

583
34:12.655 --> 34:14.824
‎Hey, Mr. Kwon, over here.

584
34:14.907 --> 34:19.078
‎♪‎ I am that person ‎No matter what anyone says‎ ♪

585
34:19.162 --> 34:21.289
‎-Yeah! ‎-♪ ‎No matter what anyone says‎ ♪

586
34:21.372 --> 34:24.292
‎-[cheering] ‎-♪ ‎More beautiful than…‎ ♪

587
34:24.375 --> 34:28.462
‎-♪‎ No matter what anyone says ‎♪ ‎-♪‎ No matter what anyone says ‎♪

588
34:28.546 --> 34:31.716
‎♪‎ Chung-hyeon is more beautiful ‎Than a flower ‎♪

589
34:31.799 --> 34:33.217
‎[laughing] Okay.

590
34:34.010 --> 34:35.928
‎-Okay. We're almost there. ‎-[yelps]

591
34:36.012 --> 34:37.597
‎Okay, okay.

592
34:37.680 --> 34:39.432
‎-[grunts] Okay, okay… ‎-[muttering]

593
34:41.726 --> 34:43.436
‎Here you go. Now I'll let you rest.

594
34:43.519 --> 34:44.770
‎-[Dr. Do] Bye! ‎-Good night.

595
34:45.771 --> 34:47.273
‎[Dr. Do] ‎He slept at the bathhouse

596
34:47.356 --> 34:50.651
‎and was waiting for us in the lobby ‎the next morning to buy us hangover soup.

597
34:50.735 --> 34:52.987
‎He even drove us ‎all the way back to Seoul.

598
34:53.070 --> 34:55.198
‎His liver? I don't know. ‎It's extraordinary.

599
34:55.281 --> 34:58.910
‎Oh, remember the last team dinner? ‎Mr. Kwon paid for everything.

600
34:58.993 --> 35:02.205
‎Even down to the designated drivers. ‎He took care of all of it.

601
35:02.288 --> 35:06.751
‎As far as these pharmaceutical reps ‎are concerned, let's show some restraint.

602
35:12.423 --> 35:15.676
‎Oh, it's just that it's ‎a long-standing tradition.

603
35:15.760 --> 35:19.513
‎At one point, there were whispers ‎about you asking a pharmaceutical employee

604
35:21.015 --> 35:22.642
‎to help with a paper you were working on.

605
35:23.434 --> 35:27.271
‎That was because it was a research paper ‎funded by that pharmaceutical company.

606
35:27.355 --> 35:28.856
‎But why were there whispers?

607
35:30.900 --> 35:32.777
‎Rumors of kickbacks.

608
35:32.860 --> 35:34.445
‎I'm sorry. I'll be more careful.

609
35:35.780 --> 35:36.864
‎Let's make sure

610
35:37.657 --> 35:39.492
‎that word is never heard in this hospital.

611
35:43.412 --> 35:45.873
‎[yawning] Let's sit here.

612
35:47.750 --> 35:49.001
‎Dr. Mun Yeong-jong.

613
35:50.836 --> 35:52.129
‎Have you been drinking this morning?

614
35:54.298 --> 35:55.675
‎What are you talking about?

615
35:56.259 --> 35:59.512
‎-He has been. ‎-Oh, yesterday I did.

616
35:59.595 --> 36:00.805
‎Can you still smell it?

617
36:01.847 --> 36:05.059
‎-I should drink a hangover cure. ‎-Last night you were working.

618
36:07.103 --> 36:10.815
‎I mean, it's not like it's ever affected ‎any of my surgeries.

619
36:10.898 --> 36:12.858
‎You could face disciplinary action.

620
36:12.942 --> 36:13.985
‎Oh, is that right?

621
36:17.238 --> 36:18.906
‎Now, you listen here, Director--

622
36:18.990 --> 36:21.492
‎Oh, Dr. Mun, this isn't the place.

623
36:24.245 --> 36:25.413
‎-[phone buzzing] ‎-Enjoy your meal.

624
36:25.496 --> 36:27.581
‎-Good day. Good day. ‎-Yeah, yeah, enjoy.

625
36:28.374 --> 36:30.293
‎Well, it's about time, Mr. Kwon--

626
36:31.335 --> 36:32.253
‎Hello?

627
36:33.504 --> 36:34.422
‎What?

628
36:34.505 --> 36:35.756
‎Well, who are you?

629
36:38.759 --> 36:39.635
‎Gye Su-jeong?

630
36:42.013 --> 36:43.431
‎You need surgery right now.

631
36:43.514 --> 36:46.600
‎-Well, I feel fine now, but thanks. ‎-That's how cholecystitis is.

632
36:46.684 --> 36:49.061
‎Over time, the pain will always come back.

633
36:49.770 --> 36:51.647
‎How about next week? Is that okay?

634
36:51.731 --> 36:53.357
‎-This week is very-- ‎-Mr. Kwon.

635
36:53.441 --> 36:55.109
‎You're familiar ‎with the healthcare industry,

636
36:55.192 --> 36:57.236
‎so why are you putting off ‎treatment of your illness?

637
36:57.820 --> 37:00.072
‎Every single doctor ‎in this hospital knows you.

638
37:00.156 --> 37:02.241
‎-I don't know him. ‎-[Dr. Kim] Now you do.

639
37:02.325 --> 37:04.952
‎Dr. Gye, thank you for helping me. ‎I was lucky you were there. Thank you.

640
37:06.579 --> 37:08.789
‎Why'd he get so mad ‎when he's the one who called?

641
37:08.873 --> 37:09.874
‎Who was mad?

642
37:12.084 --> 37:12.918
‎Dr. Do called me.

643
37:13.002 --> 37:14.879
‎Ah, the bush league surgeon.

644
37:14.962 --> 37:17.673
‎Um, did you tell Dr. Do ‎that I was here, by any chance?

645
37:18.632 --> 37:20.843
‎-Ah! ‎-[Dr. Do] No, don't get up.

646
37:22.261 --> 37:23.262
‎Uh, did you--

647
37:25.389 --> 37:27.850
‎-Did you schedule the surgery? ‎-I'm gonna do it next week.

648
37:27.933 --> 37:29.393
‎Next week? Why?

649
37:29.477 --> 37:30.478
‎This isn't your first episode.

650
37:31.062 --> 37:33.356
‎I thought it was just indigestion ‎or something.

651
37:34.774 --> 37:36.525
‎I'm sorry, Dr. Do, but…

652
37:37.610 --> 37:38.527
‎I couldn't make our meeting.

653
37:38.611 --> 37:40.988
‎Ah, no, come on. You're sick. It's okay.

654
37:41.072 --> 37:42.865
‎Put Mr. Kwon's surgery on my schedule.

655
37:42.948 --> 37:44.408
‎-Ah, well… ‎-Mmm!

656
37:45.076 --> 37:45.910
‎Oh, hey.

657
37:45.993 --> 37:47.870
‎[gasps] Hello, sir!

658
37:51.290 --> 37:54.085
‎I was looking forward to dinner tonight, ‎but I don't think I can make it.

659
37:54.168 --> 37:56.170
‎I just had a look at your ultrasound.

660
37:56.796 --> 37:58.589
‎But you've already been diagnosed ‎and you need surgery.

661
37:58.672 --> 38:01.759
‎I know. I was hoping ‎you could do my surgery.

662
38:02.968 --> 38:04.845
‎Uh, I was gonna ask you tonight.

663
38:04.929 --> 38:06.597
‎You should have had the surgery earlier.

664
38:06.680 --> 38:09.433
‎What were you thinking, Private Kwon?

665
38:12.311 --> 38:14.563
‎-[soldier 1] Oh, there he goes. ‎-[soldier 2] Whoops!

666
38:14.647 --> 38:15.981
‎Take it like a man, you little shit.

667
38:16.065 --> 38:18.984
‎-What's the matter? ‎-Need a hand? Wow.

668
38:19.068 --> 38:21.195
‎-[soldier 2] Yeah, that's a good job. ‎-[soldier 1] Okay, get ready.

669
38:21.278 --> 38:23.072
‎-[soldier 2] Focus, focus. ‎-Go.

670
38:23.155 --> 38:25.074
‎-Hey, that's good. That's good. ‎-[laughter]

671
38:25.157 --> 38:27.827
‎-Hey, no hands. ‎-[soldier 3] Come on, geez!

672
38:27.910 --> 38:29.745
‎[Kwon] ‎After my father passed away,

673
38:29.829 --> 38:32.289
‎-my family went bankrupt. ‎-Come on, man!

674
38:32.373 --> 38:33.874
‎[Kwon] ‎Since I couldn't do ‎anything to help,

675
38:33.958 --> 38:37.461
‎I figured I could at least save the family ‎money by taking a break from college

676
38:37.545 --> 38:39.422
‎and doing my military service.

677
38:40.005 --> 38:42.133
‎-All right, here we go. ‎-Open his mouth, open his mouth.

678
38:42.216 --> 38:44.260
‎-Open it, open it. ‎-[soldier 2] Open up!

679
38:44.343 --> 38:46.720
‎-[gagging] ‎-[soldiers laughing]

680
38:46.804 --> 38:48.431
‎[Kwon] ‎And that's when the nightmare began.

681
38:49.390 --> 38:51.475
‎-[choking] ‎-[water flowing]

682
38:51.559 --> 38:53.477
‎-[K-pop music playing] ‎-[laughing]

683
38:53.561 --> 38:56.772
‎-[Kwon] ‎I still don't know why… ‎-Faster, faster.

684
38:56.856 --> 38:59.984
‎-…why they bullied me so much. ‎-Do it like this. Hey! More!

685
39:00.067 --> 39:01.694
‎[Kwon] ‎They picked fights with me.

686
39:01.777 --> 39:05.156
‎Made me do exercises and beat me up.

687
39:05.239 --> 39:07.533
‎-[whimpers] ‎-Do it right, you dumbass! Geez!

688
39:07.616 --> 39:09.076
‎[Kwon] ‎It got worse and worse.

689
39:09.160 --> 39:11.787
‎-Spin! Spin! ‎-[Kwon] ‎Then one night,

690
39:11.871 --> 39:13.873
‎I couldn't take it anymore ‎and I fought back.

691
39:14.915 --> 39:17.376
‎-And that was the last straw. ‎-[soldier 2] Bastard.

692
39:18.544 --> 39:21.046
‎-[grunting] ‎-Here you go!

693
39:21.130 --> 39:23.257
‎-Little shit! ‎-One more!

694
39:23.340 --> 39:25.718
‎-[grunting] Like that? ‎-[door opens]

695
39:25.801 --> 39:27.386
‎Ah, shit.

696
39:29.889 --> 39:32.933
‎You sons of bitches. ‎What the hell are you doing?

697
39:34.351 --> 39:36.228
‎-Kwon Chung-hyeon. ‎-[groans weakly]

698
39:36.312 --> 39:37.646
‎Kwon Chung-hyeon.

699
39:40.941 --> 39:41.775
‎Private Kwon.

700
39:42.359 --> 39:44.695
‎Can you hear me? Private Kwon?

701
39:44.778 --> 39:46.447
‎-Private Kwon, hang in there. ‎-[wheezing]

702
39:47.364 --> 39:48.866
‎There's nothing we can do here.

703
39:48.949 --> 39:50.409
‎The ambulance will be here soon.

704
39:51.577 --> 39:54.914
‎The ambulance is on the way, but it'll ‎take 30 to 40 minutes to get here.

705
39:54.997 --> 39:55.831
‎What?

706
39:55.915 --> 39:59.251
‎-[Kwon wheezing] ‎-[sighs]

707
40:01.086 --> 40:02.296
‎He's bleeding internally.

708
40:03.547 --> 40:05.508
‎At this rate, ‎he won't make it to the hospital.

709
40:08.594 --> 40:09.470
‎Private Kwon.

710
40:10.179 --> 40:11.430
‎Private Kwon, can you hear me?

711
40:12.139 --> 40:12.973
‎Stay with me!

712
40:14.391 --> 40:15.976
‎Hey, Kwon Chung-hyeon, stay with me!

713
40:17.811 --> 40:18.812
‎I'm gonna save you.

714
40:19.897 --> 40:21.106
‎No matter what, I'll save you.

715
40:24.276 --> 40:25.736
‎NAMIL CLINIC

716
40:31.325 --> 40:34.954
‎Uh… any other medical staff around?

717
40:35.037 --> 40:35.955
‎No.

718
40:45.631 --> 40:46.590
‎Kwon Chung-hyeon.

719
40:47.174 --> 40:48.676
‎Kwon Chung-hyeon, wake up.

720
40:48.759 --> 40:51.595
‎You need to put those guys away. ‎Open your eyes.

721
40:53.389 --> 40:54.265
‎I'll save you.

722
40:55.349 --> 40:56.559
‎Hang in there.

723
41:00.688 --> 41:01.605
‎I'll do it.

724
41:07.111 --> 41:09.196
‎Mr. Kwon used to visit him occasionally,

725
41:09.280 --> 41:11.365
‎even after he was discharged ‎from the military.

726
41:11.448 --> 41:14.368
‎-And they always kept in touch. ‎-I can see why. Wow.

727
41:14.451 --> 41:17.079
‎That Na Dae-il, he's awesome.

728
41:17.830 --> 41:19.498
‎Mr. Kwon and I were talking one time,

729
41:19.582 --> 41:21.166
‎and he casually mentioned

730
41:21.250 --> 41:23.794
‎that he owed his life to someone he met ‎while he was enlisted.

731
41:23.877 --> 41:25.754
‎So, I thought he was just tipsy,

732
41:26.338 --> 41:29.049
‎but he said that person inspired him ‎to work in the medical field.

733
41:29.133 --> 41:31.093
‎-Hmm. ‎-So it was true.

734
41:31.176 --> 41:32.219
‎Mm-hmm.

735
41:32.303 --> 41:34.555
‎Dr. Na testified at the Center ‎for Military Human Rights.

736
41:34.638 --> 41:35.973
‎Ah! [chuckles]

737
41:36.056 --> 41:39.310
‎And that Snake Su-jeong, ‎disrespecting such a heroic doctor.

738
41:39.393 --> 41:41.895
‎You saw what she did. ‎I'm not kidding. It was terrible.

739
41:42.479 --> 41:44.773
‎So, how are you going to operate?

740
41:45.899 --> 41:47.484
‎[Dr. Bae] ‎"Are you going in laparoscopically?"

741
41:47.568 --> 41:50.362
‎Who would cut up a patient ‎when they could do it laparoscopically?

742
41:50.446 --> 41:52.823
‎And yet, last time, ‎she was the one going on and on

743
41:52.906 --> 41:54.325
‎about minimally invasive surgery.

744
41:54.408 --> 41:58.954
‎"Recovery from laparoscopic surgery ‎is quicker. I'll do the best I can."

745
41:59.872 --> 42:02.458
‎Did you see how he was beaming? ‎His face looked like the sun!

746
42:02.541 --> 42:04.043
‎[all chuckle]

747
42:04.126 --> 42:08.047
‎And to think, under those conditions, he ‎did the anesthesia and he did the surgery.

748
42:09.298 --> 42:10.299
‎He really is a hero.

749
42:11.467 --> 42:14.261
‎If you hadn't gone for the double board ‎and just done the fellowship,

750
42:14.345 --> 42:16.096
‎that would have been your spot, easy.

751
42:16.180 --> 42:17.348
‎Yeah.

752
42:17.431 --> 42:18.891
‎I don't know about that.

753
42:18.974 --> 42:21.935
‎This whole thing is the entire fault ‎of Snake Su-jeong.

754
42:22.019 --> 42:24.855
‎Everyone is all in a tizzy ‎because of her, you know?

755
42:26.857 --> 42:27.941
‎You're not quitting neurosurgery, are you?

756
42:31.779 --> 42:32.655
‎Well?

757
42:33.447 --> 42:34.948
‎It's a simple question.

758
42:36.325 --> 42:39.078
‎You can't quit! ‎You have to stay with us, man!

759
42:40.162 --> 42:43.082
‎We're just as tight ‎as Na Dae-il and Mr. Kwon.

760
42:43.957 --> 42:46.168
‎It's awfully scary to be close to people.

761
42:46.251 --> 42:49.129
‎How do make a statement like that ‎with no emotion at all?

762
42:49.213 --> 42:50.839
‎Did you have emotions as an intern?

763
42:50.923 --> 42:52.049
‎How about you, huh?

764
42:52.132 --> 42:53.634
‎-[sighs] ‎-[Dr. Do chuckles]

765
42:54.218 --> 42:56.303
‎But you have them now, don't you?

766
42:57.137 --> 42:59.223
‎He’s making me take ‎a trip down memory lane.

767
42:59.306 --> 43:00.808
‎Listen to me, Park Tae-gyeong.

768
43:01.809 --> 43:05.270
‎This guy right here ‎is just like this guy right here.

769
43:05.354 --> 43:07.106
‎-And this guy-- ‎-Nope, count me out.

770
43:07.189 --> 43:08.732
‎[laughs]

771
43:08.816 --> 43:10.484
‎I don't wanna be compared to you, either!

772
43:10.567 --> 43:12.903
‎When I was your age, ‎I was so much more impressive than you!

773
43:12.986 --> 43:14.154
‎-Huh? ‎-I really was.

774
43:14.738 --> 43:17.116
‎-In pretty much every way. ‎-Sure, sure, sure.

775
43:17.199 --> 43:18.367
‎Wow!

776
43:19.952 --> 43:21.870
‎Then my future is…

777
43:23.580 --> 43:24.998
‎-Huh? ‎-Huh?

778
43:27.334 --> 43:28.836
‎I think I'm gonna go now.

779
43:33.257 --> 43:34.633
‎-Um… ‎-What?

780
43:36.969 --> 43:38.220
‎[scoffs]

781
43:38.971 --> 43:40.305
‎So Na Dae-il will do the surgery?

782
43:41.098 --> 43:42.641
‎-Monday morning? ‎-Yeah.

783
43:42.725 --> 43:44.351
‎Wait, why are you waiting so long?

784
43:44.852 --> 43:46.437
‎MATH ACADEMY

785
43:46.520 --> 43:48.939
‎[Dr. Bae] ‎He said there was something ‎he had to do this week.

786
43:55.362 --> 43:58.699
‎You must be hungry. There's ‎gimbap‎ there. ‎Make sure to eat that first.

787
43:59.533 --> 44:00.784
‎It's tuna ‎gimbap‎, your favorite.

788
44:01.827 --> 44:03.120
‎Tell me everything you wanna eat.

789
44:05.372 --> 44:07.708
‎What do you want tomorrow? ‎Pizza from that place yesterday?

790
44:10.878 --> 44:12.671
‎Oh. [groans]

791
44:16.425 --> 44:17.760
‎Put your seat belt on.

792
44:32.733 --> 44:33.692
‎Today is…

793
44:34.777 --> 44:35.611
‎Tuesday.

794
44:37.613 --> 44:40.365
‎I'm pretty sure he won't be able to last ‎until next Monday.

795
44:40.449 --> 44:41.909
‎KWON CHUNG-HYEON

796
44:41.992 --> 44:42.993
‎Huh.

797
44:44.119 --> 44:45.287
‎What is this from?

798
45:20.239 --> 45:21.156
‎Do you know…

799
45:24.201 --> 45:26.245
‎are there are lot of surgeries ‎scheduled this week?

800
45:31.875 --> 45:32.960
‎[Dr. Na] Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

801
45:35.337 --> 45:36.880
‎[sighs] You walk fast.

802
45:38.048 --> 45:40.425
‎When they say you leave work on time, ‎they're not kidding.

803
45:41.343 --> 45:44.596
‎Even though I saw you twice today, ‎we never got to talk in private.

804
45:45.097 --> 45:47.849
‎Mr. Kwon Chung-hyeon ‎won't be able to last until Monday.

805
45:47.933 --> 45:49.893
‎That's not what I want to talk about.

806
45:50.477 --> 45:51.311
‎Uh…

807
45:53.313 --> 45:54.648
‎Uh…

808
45:54.731 --> 45:56.191
‎The thing is, um…

809
45:56.984 --> 45:57.943
‎I wanna eat a meal with you.

810
46:01.238 --> 46:02.948
‎Ah. [chuckles]

811
46:03.031 --> 46:05.158
‎That sounded so lame, I'm embarrassed.

812
46:06.702 --> 46:09.246
‎But we should eat.

813
46:10.247 --> 46:11.206
‎Together.

814
46:11.790 --> 46:14.042
‎Socializing is not something I do.

815
46:14.543 --> 46:17.296
‎What if it's not socializing, ‎what if I wanna talk about work?

816
46:17.379 --> 46:18.463
‎Then do it now.

817
46:18.547 --> 46:20.882
‎If he needs surgery before Monday, ‎will you still do it?

818
46:20.966 --> 46:22.551
‎If I'm available, then yes.

819
46:22.634 --> 46:24.803
‎-What if you aren't? ‎-Then some other doctor can do it.

820
46:26.388 --> 46:29.683
‎-Did you see the imaging? On the liver? ‎-That's…

821
46:29.766 --> 46:33.478
‎most likely just a minor adhesion that ‎formed due to his surgery years ago.

822
46:34.896 --> 46:36.064
‎But you never know.

823
46:36.148 --> 46:37.733
‎Well, I doubt that it's a tumor.

824
46:37.816 --> 46:39.318
‎You'll have to open him up to find out.

825
46:43.864 --> 46:47.117
‎I watched the footage of your surgery. ‎I've never seen anything like it.

826
46:47.743 --> 46:50.037
‎If I were the patient, ‎I'd want you as my surgeon.

827
46:51.038 --> 46:52.748
‎It was truly amazing.

828
46:53.332 --> 46:55.584
‎It seemed like you were a god.

829
47:01.548 --> 47:03.592
‎Or a monster. [chuckles]

830
47:06.345 --> 47:08.013
‎I heard that you leap before you look.

831
47:08.764 --> 47:10.390
‎That made me curious as to…

832
47:11.600 --> 47:12.851
‎what you’re leaping into.

833
47:14.102 --> 47:15.354
‎I leap before I look?

834
47:15.437 --> 47:17.230
‎According to Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

835
47:19.483 --> 47:20.400
‎He doesn't know me.

836
47:25.322 --> 47:26.782
‎Then is it behind you?

837
47:28.116 --> 47:31.411
‎Is there something behind you ‎that makes you leap before you look?

838
47:49.680 --> 47:52.307
‎[sighs] I guess I don't know Dr. Gye.

839
47:55.519 --> 47:56.978
‎Oh, come on.

840
48:01.274 --> 48:02.609
‎Ah.

841
48:14.079 --> 48:15.539
‎[chimes]

842
48:35.392 --> 48:37.602
‎[clock ticking]

843
48:57.080 --> 48:58.081
‎[Ms. Jang] Su-jeong!

844
49:03.086 --> 49:05.547
‎Oh, nice! Go make us some money.

845
49:08.884 --> 49:10.260
‎WEDNESDAY ‎8:10 A.M.

846
49:10.343 --> 49:17.350
‎WEDNESDAY ‎8:31 A.M.

847
49:18.977 --> 49:19.936
‎Shall we go in?

848
49:24.191 --> 49:25.192
‎Thank you, miss!

849
49:41.374 --> 49:42.209
‎[trainer] Go!

850
49:42.292 --> 49:44.294
‎WEDNESDAY ‎7:45 P.M.

851
49:44.377 --> 49:45.212
‎Nice.

852
50:04.314 --> 50:05.982
‎[Dr. Na] Next, Choi Ha-il,

853
50:06.483 --> 50:07.859
‎a 56-year-old male.

854
50:08.401 --> 50:12.030
‎He is a severe alcoholic and has history ‎of drinking two bottles of soju per day.

855
50:12.113 --> 50:16.076
‎He was diagnosed with cirrhosis ‎of the liver, but was lost to follow-up.

856
50:17.744 --> 50:21.915
‎He reportedly developed jaundice ‎a month ago and ascites about a week ago,

857
50:21.998 --> 50:23.667
‎which prompted his visit to the ER.

858
50:24.417 --> 50:25.919
‎Tests performed upon admission

859
50:26.002 --> 50:28.004
‎showed uncompensated liver cirrhosis,

860
50:28.088 --> 50:31.258
‎Child-Pugh Class C, ‎and a MELD score of 34.

861
50:31.341 --> 50:33.218
‎He is expected to undergo ‎a liver transplant.

862
50:33.301 --> 50:40.100
‎THURSDAY ‎3:31 P.M.

863
50:44.062 --> 50:47.315
‎THURSDAY ‎3:32 P.M.

864
50:47.399 --> 50:53.572
‎FRIDAY ‎5:44 P.M.

865
51:01.121 --> 51:02.622
‎[chuckles] Is this my seat?

866
51:06.167 --> 51:08.837
‎You know, I've loved seaweed soup ‎since I was a kid.

867
51:08.920 --> 51:14.593
‎FRIDAY ‎7:38 P.M.

868
51:14.676 --> 51:19.681
‎FRIDAY ‎7:39 P.M.

869
51:19.764 --> 51:21.057
‎Huh? What the--

870
51:23.310 --> 51:24.394
‎[gasps]

871
51:25.020 --> 51:25.854
‎DAD

872
51:26.980 --> 51:27.981
‎Come on, pick up.

873
51:28.064 --> 51:29.357
‎[groans]

874
51:32.986 --> 51:39.993
‎FRIDAY ‎7:50 P.M.

875
51:42.412 --> 51:45.832
‎All right, let us raise a glass to ‎Dr. Na Dae-il. A toast to a new beginning!

876
51:45.916 --> 51:47.459
‎[all] Cheers!

877
51:48.084 --> 51:49.920
‎-Please take good care of me. ‎-[all laugh]

878
51:52.088 --> 51:53.798
‎[Magnolia member] ‎"Please take good care of me."

879
51:54.466 --> 51:55.842
‎[Dr. Na] I wanna thank you all

880
51:55.926 --> 51:59.721
‎for giving me this precious gold ‎Magnolia badge.

881
52:00.430 --> 52:02.891
‎-I always wanted one of these. ‎-[all laugh]

882
52:02.974 --> 52:03.892
‎[groaning]

883
52:03.975 --> 52:06.728
‎FRIDAY ‎8:15 P.M.

884
52:06.811 --> 52:08.063
‎-Dad? ‎-Get out.

885
52:15.362 --> 52:16.696
‎[boy] Dad, what about ‎my after-school class?

886
52:16.780 --> 52:18.156
‎DR. JO GUK-JIN ‎ME &amp; LIFE PLASTIC SURGERY

887
52:19.616 --> 52:21.451
‎I'm swamped right now. ‎You'll have to miss it.

888
52:23.203 --> 52:24.454
‎I need an ambulance.

889
52:24.537 --> 52:26.331
‎-I'm in front of Taeseong Academy. ‎-Please!

890
52:26.414 --> 52:29.876
‎FRIDAY ‎8:16 P.M.

891
52:30.377 --> 52:32.212
‎FRIDAY ‎8:55 P.M.

892
52:32.295 --> 52:33.630
‎[groans]

893
52:35.173 --> 52:36.508
‎MARCH 20, 2026 ‎FRIDAY, 8:55 P.M.

894
52:37.759 --> 52:38.760
‎[gasps]

895
52:40.595 --> 52:42.764
‎-What are you still doing here? ‎-[phone rings]

896
52:43.473 --> 52:46.059
‎-This is the ER at Seonam Medical Center. ‎-[siren wailing]

897
52:46.142 --> 52:48.561
‎[paramedic] The driver of a dump truck ‎fell asleep at the wheel.

898
52:48.645 --> 52:50.063
‎We have 20 patients at the scene,

899
52:50.146 --> 52:52.649
‎but we've only brought 12 here so far. ‎More on the way.

900
52:52.732 --> 52:54.693
‎Dr. Kim, Dr. Kim! ‎Take this patient, please!

901
52:55.860 --> 52:58.947
‎Clear out the minor injuries to make room, ‎empty the treatment room,

902
52:59.030 --> 53:01.491
‎and move any stable critical care patients ‎to the general ward.

903
53:01.574 --> 53:03.618
‎-And page the interns, right now. ‎-[phone ringing]

904
53:03.702 --> 53:05.537
‎-[nurse] Will do. ‎-Dr. Gye, this patient--

905
53:05.620 --> 53:07.247
‎[nurse] All interns to the ER.

906
53:10.166 --> 53:12.210
‎-[guests laughing, chattering] ‎-[phone buzzing]

907
53:19.759 --> 53:21.886
‎Uh, Chairman, excuse me for one moment.

908
53:26.057 --> 53:28.518
‎Hello, Dr. Kim. How can I help you?

909
53:29.853 --> 53:30.687
‎Sorry?

910
53:33.023 --> 53:34.482
‎Ah, yes, Mr. Kwon.

911
53:36.151 --> 53:37.485
‎Okay, I'll be there soon.

912
53:38.069 --> 53:42.282
‎Although, I'm out at the moment and I ‎don't know if I'll make it there in time.

913
53:42.365 --> 53:43.992
‎Maybe there's another doctor available.

914
53:47.454 --> 53:48.955
‎Really? Dr. Gye?

915
53:49.581 --> 53:50.832
‎But… why her?

916
53:53.585 --> 53:55.378
‎I doubt she's available right now.

917
53:55.462 --> 53:57.255
‎-[staff clamoring] ‎-Yeah, there's no one else who can do it.

918
53:57.338 --> 53:59.257
‎The ER's out of control. ‎There was a major car accident.

919
53:59.340 --> 54:00.884
‎All the other doctors are down here,

920
54:00.967 --> 54:03.178
‎-so she's getting ready to do the surgery… ‎-[nurse] Yes, just a moment.

921
54:03.261 --> 54:04.387
‎What?

922
54:05.221 --> 54:06.139
‎I can't hear you.

923
54:07.015 --> 54:09.017
‎Mr. Kwon's fever is too high right now.

924
54:09.100 --> 54:11.352
‎-Sorry, what can't be done? ‎-[phones ringing]

925
54:11.436 --> 54:13.813
‎What? Uh, excuse me, Dr. Na? Hang on.

926
54:15.065 --> 54:16.399
‎Dr. Gye, what's going on?

927
54:17.317 --> 54:18.193
‎What?

928
54:18.693 --> 54:21.071
‎You can't get in the OR? ‎The fingerprint scanner doesn't work?

929
54:21.780 --> 54:22.864
‎Why isn't it working?

930
54:22.947 --> 54:24.407
‎Uh, just hang on a minute.

931
54:24.866 --> 54:26.451
‎-Dr. Na, right now, uh-- ‎-[call disconnects]

932
54:26.534 --> 54:28.161
‎[Director Kim] ‎When was the last time you hit the links?

933
54:28.244 --> 54:32.123
‎-Oh, I try to play once or twice a month. ‎-There's also a good course here.

934
54:32.207 --> 54:34.542
‎[Chairman Kim] ‎Wow, I'd love to, just let me know when.

935
54:35.293 --> 54:38.213
‎-[member 1] Save it for the next meeting. ‎-[member 2] Come to my place.

936
54:38.296 --> 54:42.050
‎Dr. Gye! Dr. Gye! ‎I heard you need my finger--

937
54:42.133 --> 54:44.010
‎-[beeps] ‎-There we go.

938
54:46.137 --> 54:47.138
‎You, assist me.

939
54:47.222 --> 54:48.098
‎Oh, okay. Coming.

940
54:48.890 --> 54:50.350
‎Isn't there anyone else available?

941
54:50.433 --> 54:51.768
‎Only Dr. Jo Won-jin.

942
54:51.851 --> 54:53.561
‎They're all downstairs ‎because of the accident.

943
54:53.645 --> 54:56.981
‎I don't want to wait for an assistant, ‎so you'll do. I want to do it right away.

944
54:59.943 --> 55:00.777
‎Or no?

945
55:00.860 --> 55:03.154
‎[stammering] I'll do it.

946
55:03.238 --> 55:04.239
‎[chuckles]

947
55:06.658 --> 55:07.700
‎Uh…

948
55:08.910 --> 55:11.788
‎[monitors beeping]

949
55:11.871 --> 55:15.917
‎[Dr. Jo] I can't believe those surgeons! ‎Deleting your fingerprint registration?

950
55:16.000 --> 55:18.878
‎Also, I could've just gone out and opened ‎the door. Why'd you chase after her?

951
55:22.090 --> 55:23.675
‎[Dr. Park] Oh, you're opening him up?

952
55:23.758 --> 55:25.760
‎[Dr. Jo] ‎There's severe adhesion. And what else?

953
55:25.844 --> 55:27.929
‎[Dr. Gye] ‎I'll have to open him up to find out.

954
55:34.769 --> 55:37.605
‎[laughing, chattering]

955
55:42.193 --> 55:43.486
‎[Dr. Kim] ‎This is Kim Seong-jin.

956
55:43.570 --> 55:45.613
‎We're opening him up. ‎There's likely to be severe adhesion.

957
55:45.697 --> 55:48.950
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong will take care of him, ‎so I don't think we'll need you here.

958
55:53.788 --> 55:55.665
‎I have to go do an emergency surgery.

959
55:55.748 --> 55:57.584
‎Oh, of course. We understand.

960
55:57.667 --> 55:59.419
‎-What's with him? ‎-[all laugh]

961
56:04.591 --> 56:05.675
‎[Dr. Gye] Bovie.

962
56:06.593 --> 56:07.635
‎[Dr. Park] Bovie.

963
56:37.165 --> 56:39.792
‎-[dramatic music playing] ‎-[horns honking]

964
56:39.876 --> 56:44.505
‎Man. There was a huge accident. ‎Traffic is at a standstill.

965
56:44.589 --> 56:46.049
‎We're gonna be here for a while.

966
56:56.184 --> 56:57.977
‎[phone ringing]

967
57:01.314 --> 57:04.525
‎DR. NA DAE-IL

968
58:02.333 --> 58:03.835
‎Damn it, Gye Su-jeong.

969
58:03.918 --> 58:05.503
‎[grunting]

970
58:05.587 --> 58:07.589
‎[dramatic music continues]

971
58:16.848 --> 58:18.850
‎[music stops]

972
58:39.412 --> 58:40.580
‎Huh.

973
58:42.582 --> 58:45.001
‎[grunting]

974
58:45.084 --> 58:47.920
‎[downbeat pop music playing]

975
59:26.542 --> 59:29.504
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

976
59:29.587 --> 59:33.007
‎[music continues]

977
01:00:14.632 --> 01:00:17.593
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

978
01:00:17.677 --> 01:00:19.053
‎[Dr. Na humming]

979
01:00:19.137 --> 01:00:21.639
‎[Dr. Park] ‎They're initials, right? ‎I'm not the only one who sees this, right?

980
01:00:21.723 --> 01:00:23.391
‎-You'll let the hospital know? ‎-[Dr. Gye]‎ No.

981
01:00:23.474 --> 01:00:24.976
‎This hospital brought him in.

982
01:00:25.059 --> 01:00:28.688
‎[Kwon] ‎Why did you show me the picture? ‎There's nothing I can do.

983
01:00:28.771 --> 01:00:30.189
‎Get away from him. He's my patient.

984
01:00:30.690 --> 01:00:33.276
‎[Dr. Na] ‎He's alive, thanks to you. ‎It's such a relief.

985
01:00:33.860 --> 01:00:35.778
‎[Dr. Gye] ‎I wish you hadn't said that.

986
01:00:35.862 --> 01:00:36.988
‎-Where is she? Your teacher. ‎-[gasps]

987
01:00:37.071 --> 01:00:40.116
‎[Director Bu] ‎I think the time ‎has truly come to terminate the contract.

988
01:00:40.700 --> 01:00:45.037
‎Don't worry. ‎One thing's for sure, I never fail.
